# Normalise text to LF in the repository, so a contributor whose git has
# core.autocrlf=true cannot rewrite whole files. The app targets Windows, and LF
# in the repository is fine for MSBuild, the C# compiler, PowerShell 7 and
# Git for Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch.
*.bmp binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.zip binary

# Files committed before this file existed are a mix of LF and CRLF. A single
# `git add --renormalize .` brings the index in line; until then, the first commit
# that touches one of those files will show it as wholly changed.
